---
import LegalLayout from '../layouts/LegalLayout.astro';
import { useTranslations } from '../i18n/ui';

const t = useTranslations('en');
---

<LegalLayout
  lang="en"
  title={t.meta.kvkk.title}
  description={t.meta.kvkk.description}
  path="/kvkk/"
  heading="Data Protection Notice (GDPR)"
  updated="Last updated: July 2026"
>
  <p>
    This notice explains how Leviora processes personal data collected through leviora.ai,
    in line with the EU General Data Protection Regulation ("GDPR"). For visitors in
    Türkiye, the Turkish notice under Law No. 6698 (KVKK) is available at
    <a href="/tr/kvkk/">/tr/kvkk/</a>.
  </p>

  <h2>1. Controller</h2>
  <p>
    Leviora is the controller of the personal data described in this notice. Contact:
    <a href="mailto:info@leviora.ai">info@leviora.ai</a>.
  </p>

  <h2>2. Personal data we process and why</h2>
  <p>
    When you submit the demo request form, we process the identity and contact data you
    provide — name, email address, phone number, company and your message — to respond to
    your request, schedule a demo or pilot, and carry out related business communication.
    Our web servers also keep standard technical logs (IP address, request time, requested
    page) for security and operations.
  </p>

  <h2>3. Legal bases</h2>
  <p>
    We rely on Article 6(1)(b) GDPR — steps taken at your request prior to entering into a
    contract — for handling your demo request, and on Article 6(1)(f) GDPR — our legitimate
    interest in operating and securing the website — for technical logs.
  </p>

  <h2>4. Recipients and international transfers</h2>
  <p>
    Form submissions are delivered to us through an email infrastructure provider
    established in the United States; the transfer is protected by appropriate safeguards
    under Article 46 GDPR (standard contractual clauses). We do not sell personal data and
    we do not share it for third-party marketing.
  </p>

  <h2>5. Retention</h2>
  <p>
    If no business relationship is established, demo request data is deleted no later than
    24 months after your request is closed, unless a legal obligation requires longer
    storage. Technical logs are kept for a short, rolling period.
  </p>

  <h2>6. Your rights</h2>
  <p>
    Under Articles 15–21 GDPR you may request access to, rectification or erasure of your
    personal data, restriction of processing, data portability, and you may object to
    processing based on legitimate interest. To exercise these rights, write to
    <a href="mailto:info@leviora.ai">info@leviora.ai</a>. You also have the right to lodge
    a complaint with your local supervisory authority.
  </p>
</LegalLayout>
